            <ArticleTitle>A case of &quot;silent&quot; pheochromocytoma presenting as spontaneous retroperitoneal hematoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>735-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pheochromocytoma of the adrenal gland can be the cause of massive and lethal retroperitoneal haemorrhage presenting as acute abdomen. Here we report a case of retroperitoneal hematoma, with concomitant peritoneal spillage, due to the spontaneous rupture of a silent pheochromocytoma. The main clinical findings of this disease will be described. Therapy and prognosis will be also discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
